  "description": "The most notable feature of a gut knife is the gut hook on the spine of the blade.  Originally popularized as an aid for field dressing game, the gut hook is also effective at  cutting through fibrous materials like rope, webbing, or safety belts with ease. It has individual parts spray-painted solid colors in a black and purple color scheme.\\n\\n<i>Elegant design paired with brutal intent</i>",
